Enhancement: lock parity Phase 5 revalidated minimal-lock forget

Forget now evaluates retention and delete protection under a shared/read phase,
then re-lists and re-evaluates under a short exclusive deletion phase. It only
removes snapshot IDs selected by both observations. Snapshots created, newly
protected, or no longer selected while policy evaluation runs are retained.

`forget --prune` keeps its established exclusive handoff into prune. An
integration test pauses forget phase A, completes a backup, then confirms that
the new snapshot survives phase-B revalidation and the repository remains
clean after prune/check.

